# Everything is excluded, then the few things the image needs are allowed back
# in. A denylist is the wrong default here: the repository root is where
# `veritas-agent up` writes a wallet keystore *and its plaintext passphrase*
# (see veritas/autonomous/wallet.py), so a forgotten pattern is a private key
# in a published image, not a slow build.
#
# This also keeps the build context small: without it, `docker build` uploads
# the runtime directory, the ledger database and every receipt to the daemon
# before the first instruction runs.
*

!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!requirements.lock
!veritas/

# Re-exclude things that live inside the allowed paths.
veritas/**/__pycache__/
veritas/**/*.py[cod]
